{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA: f124's commit 1d75850974 and the comment-hygiene gate (b047, f2b2d0b410) were in Gerrit review concurrently; f124 merged ~10 min after the gate landed, so its three bare run-id citations never passed through it. The whole-tree lint then failed every subsequent patchset (1309 ps4, 1311 ps3). Fix: replace the run-id tokens with durable prose citing the f124 incident ticket — pushed as Gerrit change 1313. This is the by-design residual of a whole-tree gate: concurrent in-flight changes are linted against the tree they were written on; first rebase/recheck after the offending merge surfaces it, and the fix is one durable-citation edit."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785789103939148001,"uuid":"d29536d9-af8a-4737-aa8e-9e09a5e65a56"}